    "narrative": "Today\u2019s limited slate leaves LawDog with a narrow path to point maximization, as the heavy hitters like **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Bryce Harper**, **Cal Raleigh**, and **Lawrence Butler** are all sidelined by team off-days. With our bench depleted, **Will Smith** remains our primary anchor. His 51.12 score reflects a marginal start, constrained largely by his #7 position in the order against Gasser. While the matchup against a 4.14 xERA arm isn't prohibitive, the lack of lineup leverage for **Will Smith** keeps him in the lower end of our starting tier; we are relying on his xwOBA of 0.389 to provide the necessary floor to avoid wasting a precious game cap.\n\nThe bench construction today is effectively forced by the schedule, but the proximity of our depth options\u2014specifically the versatility of **Brendan Donovan** and **Masyn Winn**\u2014highlights the risk of over-exposure on light days. If we had a full slate, **Justin Crawford** and **Dylan Beavers** would have been primary targets for their stolen base potential; in this scoring environment, they represent the high-upside plays we are currently missing. Without **Yainer Diaz**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Matt Chapman**, **Daulton Varsho**, **Luis Arraez**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **JJ Bleday**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Zack Gelof**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Braden Montgomery** active or in favorable spots, our strategy is purely defensive. Monitor the official lineups for **Will Smith**; if he drops further in the order or if the weather shifts in his hitter-friendly park, we should pivot to benching him entirely to preserve the cap for high-leverage outcomes later in the week.",
